      <li>2325 3rd Street, Suite 215, San Francisco, California 94107, United States</li>
      <li>Support: <a href="mailto:support@netlify.com">support@netlify.com</a></li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Intellectual property</h2>
    <p>All elements of the site (text, graphics, logos, images, videos, structure and layout) are the exclusive property of Advised by Francis Ndimba, unless otherwise stated or where content belongs to partners. Any reproduction, distribution, modification, adaptation, retransmission or publication, even in part, of these elements is prohibited without the prior written consent of the publisher.</p>

    <h2 id="personal-data">4. Personal data (GDPR)</h2>
    <p>In the context of enquiries and browsing, the following data may be collected: surname, first name, email address and browsing data.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Data controller: Francis Ndimba</li>
      <li>Purpose: responding to enquiries, commercial relationship and site improvement</li>
      <li>Retention period: 3 years maximum from the last contact</li>
      <li>Your rights: access, rectification, erasure, objection, restriction and portability of your data</li>
    </ul>
    <p>To exercise these rights, write to <a href="mailto:contact@advised-seo.fr">contact@advised-seo.fr</a>. You also have the right to lodge a complaint with the French data protection authority, the CNIL (<a href="https://www.cnil.fr/en" target="_blank" rel="noopener">cnil.fr</a>).</p>

    <h2>5. Cookies</h2>
    <p>The site may use cookies for audience measurement and to improve the user experience. You can configure or refuse cookies directly from your browser settings.</p>

    <h2>6. Liability</h2>
    <p>The publisher strives to provide accurate, up-to-date information, without however guaranteeing completeness or the absence of error. The site may contain links to third-party sites, over whose content the publisher exercises no control and for which it declines all responsibility.</p>

    <h2>7. Governing law</h2>
    <p>This site and its legal notice are governed by French law. In the event of a dispute, and failing an amicable resolution, jurisdiction is granted to the French courts.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .legal { max-width: 780px; }
  .legal .updated { font-size: 14px; color: var(--ink-45); margin: 0 0 36px; }
  .legal h2 { font-size: clamp(22px, 2.6vw, 30px); margin: 48px 0 14px; }
  .legal p { color: var(--ink-60); font-size: 16.5px; line-height: 1.75; margin: 0 0 14px; text-wrap: pretty; }
  .legal ul { color: var(--ink-60); font-size: 16.5px; line-height: 1.7; margin: 0 0 18px; padding-left: 1.15em; }
  .legal li { margin-bottom: 7px; }
  .legal strong { color: var(--blue); font-weight: 600; }
  .legal a { color: var(--orange); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
  .legal a:hover { color: var(--orange-deep); }
</style>
</Base>
